WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.420
What is your earliest memory of Mossville?

2
00:00:03.420 --> 00:00:06.300
Oh, I forgot what year that I came down here.

3
00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:09.280
It was way back when.

4
00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:14.040
Old Spanish Trail was just a one-way highway.

5
00:00:14.040 --> 00:00:19.340
When you meet another car, one of them had to get off and . . . [Laughs] Way back there.

6
00:00:19.340 --> 00:00:22.160
I’ve been here over sixty-some years.

7
00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:25.680
But anyway, I raised all my kid right here, nine kids.

8
00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:28.120
So what did Mossville look like when you came here?

9
00:00:28.120 --> 00:00:29.160
Like, so were you a teenager?

10
00:00:29.160 --> 00:00:30.640
There were very few houses.

11
00:00:30.640 --> 00:00:36.240
This used to be . . . the schoolhouse used to be right in the front of my house here, yeah.

12
00:00:36.240 --> 00:00:41.520
The schoolhouse, yeah, that was a two-story building, one teacher.

13
00:00:41.520 --> 00:00:44.240
One teacher, yeah.

14
00:00:44.240 --> 00:00:50.600
And Mossville had, like, a water trough, the kids go wash their hands and face and things right there in the yard.

15
00:00:50.600 --> 00:00:53.600
Yeah, one teacher.

16
00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:55.220
And the teacher name was Mrs. Lemelle.

17
00:00:55.220 --> 00:00:57.440
I don't know her real name.

18
00:00:57.440 --> 00:01:03.160
Mrs. Lemelle, yeah.

19
00:01:03.160 --> 00:01:07.240
And I bought this place here just passing through here.

20
00:01:07.240 --> 00:01:11.660
I got a job at Conoco and I worked there until I retired.
